  "about": "A chat photo's ThumbHash (spec/chat.md, Photos), as Evan Wallace's reference (https://github.com/evanw/thumbhash) makes and draws it. `encode`: an image of `width` by `height` (at most 100 each), its pixels `rgba` row by row, not premultiplied, as base64, and the ThumbHash its sender makes of it, as base64; its pixels are uneven, as a photo's are, so no term lands on a rounding half, which would round differently from one platform to the next. `decode`: a ThumbHash and the blur it draws, `width` by `height` (at most 32 each) and its pixels `rgba` as base64; each byte may differ by 1, as cosines round differently from one platform to the next.",
